{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019pF7BZUC7Ym1RhiRR4weyK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tuse itertools::Itertools;\n2\tuse openvm_cuda_common::{copy::MemCopyH2D, d_buffer::DeviceBuffer};\n3\tuse openvm_stark_backend::{\n4\t    air_builders::symbolic::{\n5\t        symbolic_expression::SymbolicExpression, SymbolicConstraints, SymbolicDagBuilder,\n6\t        SymbolicExpressionDag,\n7\t    },\n8\t    prover::{fractional_sumcheck_gkr::Frac, DeviceStarkProvingKey},\n9\t};\n10\tuse p3_field::PrimeCharacteristicRing;\n11\tuse tracing::{debug, warn};\n12\t\n13\tuse super::errors::Round0EvalError;\n14\tuse crate::{\n15\t    cuda::logup_zerocheck::{\n16\t        _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size, _logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size,\n17\t        _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size, _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size,\n18\t        logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0, zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints,\n19\t    },\n20\t    gpu_backend::GenericGpuBackend,\n21\t    hash_scheme::GpuHashScheme,\n22\t    logup_zerocheck::rules::{codec::Codec, SymbolicRulesGpu},\n23\t    prelude::{EF, F},\n24\t};\n25\t\n26\t/// Evaluate plain AIR constraints (not interactions) for a single AIR, given prepared trace input.\n27\t///\n28\t/// `num_cosets` should equal `constraint_degree - 1` because we evaluate the quotient polynomial.\n29\t/// See [`crate::logup_zerocheck`] module docs for async-free/peak memory behavior.\n30\t#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n31\tpub fn evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n32\t    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n33\t    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n34\t    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n35\t    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n36\t    eq_cube: *const EF,\n37\t    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n38\t    skip_domain: u32,\n39\t    num_x: u32,\n40\t    height: u32,\n41\t    num_cosets: u32,\n42\t    g_shift: F,\n43\t    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n44\t) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<EF>, Round0EvalError> {\n45\t    let constraints_dag = &pk.vk.symbolic_constraints;\n46\t    if constraints_dag.constraints.constraint_idx.is_empty() || num_cosets == 0 {\n47\t        // No plain AIR constraints, return empty buffer\n48\t        return Ok(DeviceBuffer::new());\n49\t    }\n50\t\n51\t    let rules = &pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0;\n52\t\n53\t    let buffer_size: u32 = rules.inner.buffer_size;\n54\t    let intermed_capacity = unsafe {\n55\t        _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n56\t            buffer_size,\n57\t            skip_domain,\n58\t            num_x,\n59\t            num_cosets,\n60\t            max_temp_bytes,\n61\t        )\n62\t    };\n63\t    let mut intermediates = if intermed_capacity > 0 {\n64\t        debug!(\"zerocheck:intermediates_capacity={intermed_capacity}\");\n65\t        DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)\n66\t    } else {\n67\t        DeviceBuffer::<F>::new()\n68\t    };\n69\t\n70\t    let temp_sums_buffer_capacity = unsafe {\n71\t        _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n72\t            buffer_size,\n73\t            skip_domain,\n74\t            num_x,\n75\t            num_cosets,\n76\t            max_temp_bytes,\n77\t        )\n78\t    };\n79\t    debug!(\"zerocheck:temp_sums_buffer_capacity={temp_sums_buffer_capacity}\");\n80\t    let mut temp_sums_buffer = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(temp_sums_buffer_capacity);\n81\t    let used_temp_bytes =\n82\t        intermed_capacity * size_of::<F>() + temp_sums_buffer_capacity * size_of::<EF>();\n83\t    if used_temp_bytes > max_temp_bytes {\n84\t        // We do not error if the required bytes is greater than the requested max, but this may\n85\t        // lead to unexpected peak memory usage.\n86\t        warn!(\"zerocheck used_temp_bytes ({used_temp_bytes}) > max_temp_bytes ({max_temp_bytes})\");\n87\t    }\n88\t\n89\t    let preprocessed_ptr = pk\n90\t        .preprocessed_data\n91\t        .as_ref()\n92\t        .map(|cd| cd.trace.buffer().as_ptr())\n93\t        .unwrap_or(std::ptr::null());\n94\t\n95\t    let mut sp_evals =\n96\t        DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(num_cosets as usize * skip_domain as usize);\n97\t    // SAFETY:\n98\t    // - No bounds checks are done in this kernel. It fully assumes that the Rules are trusted and\n99\t    //   all nodes are valid.\n100\t    unsafe {\n101\t        zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints(\n102\t            &mut temp_sums_buffer,\n103\t            &mut sp_evals,\n104\t            selectors_cube,\n105\t            preprocessed_ptr,\n106\t            main_parts,\n107\t            eq_cube,\n108\t            lambda_pows,\n109\t            public_values,\n110\t            &rules.inner.d_rules,\n111\t            &rules.inner.d_used_nodes,\n112\t            buffer_size,\n113\t            &mut intermediates,\n114\t            skip_domain,\n115\t            num_x,\n116\t            height,\n117\t            num_cosets,\n118\t            g_shift,\n119\t            max_temp_bytes,\n120\t        )?;\n121\t    }\n122\t\n123\t    Ok(sp_evals)\n124\t}\n125\t\n126\t/// Evaluate interaction constraints (excluding plain AIR constraints) for a single AIR, given\n127\t/// prepared trace input.\n128\t///\n129\t/// `constraints` includes interaction expressions for the AIR.\n130\t/// See [`crate::logup_zerocheck`] module docs for async-free/peak memory behavior.\n131\t#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n132\tpub fn evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n133\t    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n134\t    symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>,\n135\t    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n136\t    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n137\t    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n138\t    eq_cube: *const EF,\n139\t    beta_pows: &[EF],\n140\t    eq_3bs: &[EF],\n141\t    skip_domain: u32,\n142\t    num_x: u32,\n143\t    height: u32,\n144\t    num_cosets: u32,\n145\t    g_shift: F,\n146\t    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n147\t) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, Round0EvalError> {\n148\t    // Check if this trace has interactions\n149\t    if eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n150\t        return Ok(DeviceBuffer::new());\n151\t    }\n152\t    let large_domain = num_cosets * skip_domain;\n153\t\n154\t    // We create a new \"interactions DAG\" where the new .constraints are the interaction [count,\n155\t    // message_0, message_1, ..] expressions themselves, while the .interactions are empty\n156\t    // We track the indices with InteractionNode\n157\t\n158\t    // Copied from build_symbolic_constraints_dag to handle sorting of constraints\n159\t    // NOTE: For logup round0, the kernel uses weights indexed by rule_idx, not constraint_idx.\n160\t    // So we deduplicate constraint_idx and use dag_idx_to_rule_idx for weight mapping.\n161\t    let (rules, d_numer_weights, d_denom_weights, denom_sum_init) = {\n162\t        let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n163\t        let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n164\t        for interaction in &symbolic.interactions {\n165\t            let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n166\t            sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n167\t            sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n168\t                interaction\n169\t                    .message\n170\t                    .iter()\n171\t                    .map(|field_expr| dag_builder.add_expr(field_expr)),\n172\t            );\n173\t        }\n174\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n175\t        // Deduplicate for the dag since logup round0 kernel doesn't use used_nodes\n176\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n177\t        let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n178\t            nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n179\t            constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n180\t        };\n181\t        let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n182\t        let mut numer_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; rules.rules.len()];\n183\t        let mut denom_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; rules.rules.len()];\n184\t        let mut denom_sum_init = EF::ZERO;\n185\t        for (interaction_idx, interaction) in symbolic.interactions.iter().enumerate() {\n186\t            // CAUTION: an expression node could be used in multiple interactions, and might even be\n187\t            // used as `count` in one, but message field in another. We only care about their\n188\t            // weighted sum with eq_3b, so we compute the weights ahead of time.\n189\t            let count_dag_idx =\n190\t                dag_builder.expr_to_idx[&(&interaction.count as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n191\t            let count_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&count_dag_idx];\n192\t            numer_weights[count_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx];\n193\t            denom_sum_init += eq_3bs[interaction_idx]\n194\t                * beta_pows[interaction.message.len()]\n195\t                * F::from_u32(interaction.bus_index as u32 + 1);\n196\t\n197\t            for (message_idx, message) in interaction.message.iter().enumerate() {\n198\t                let message_dag_idx =\n199\t                    dag_builder.expr_to_idx[&(message as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n200\t                let message_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&message_dag_idx];"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e16bd043-1446-4590-8b8f-e55946754639","uuid":"13772692-92c6-472b-8bda-bae2857627f8","timestamp":"2026-04-13T05:12:16.419Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs","content":"use itertools::Itertools;\nuse openvm_cuda_common::{copy::MemCopyH2D, d_buffer::DeviceBuffer};\nuse openvm_stark_backend::{\n    air_builders::symbolic::{\n        symbolic_expression::SymbolicExpression, SymbolicConstraints, SymbolicDagBuilder,\n        SymbolicExpressionDag,\n    },\n    prover::{fractional_sumcheck_gkr::Frac, DeviceStarkProvingKey},\n};\nuse p3_field::PrimeCharacteristicRing;\nuse tracing::{debug, warn};\n\nuse super::errors::Round0EvalError;\nuse crate::{\n    cuda::logup_zerocheck::{\n        _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size, _logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size,\n        _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size, _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size,\n        logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0, zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints,\n    },\n    gpu_backend::GenericGpuBackend,\n    hash_scheme::GpuHashScheme,\n    logup_zerocheck::rules::{codec::Codec, SymbolicRulesGpu},\n    prelude::{EF, F},\n};\n\n/// Evaluate plain AIR constraints (not interactions) for a single AIR, given prepared trace input.\n///\n/// `num_cosets` should equal `constraint_degree - 1` because we evaluate the quotient polynomial.\n/// See [`crate::logup_zerocheck`] module docs for async-free/peak memory behavior.\n#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\npub fn evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<EF>, Round0EvalError> {\n    let constraints_dag = &pk.vk.symbolic_constraints;\n    if constraints_dag.constraints.constraint_idx.is_empty() || num_cosets == 0 {\n        // No plain AIR constraints, return empty buffer\n        return Ok(DeviceBuffer::new());\n    }\n\n    let rules = &pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0;\n\n    let buffer_size: u32 = rules.inner.buffer_size;\n    let intermed_capacity = unsafe {\n        _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n            buffer_size,\n            skip_domain,\n            num_x,\n            num_cosets,\n            max_temp_bytes,\n        )\n    };\n    let mut intermediates = if intermed_capacity > 0 {\n        debug!(\"zerocheck:intermediates_capacity={intermed_capacity}\");\n        DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)\n    } else {\n        DeviceBuffer::<F>::new()\n    };\n\n    let temp_sums_buffer_capacity = unsafe {\n        _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n            buffer_size,\n            skip_domain,\n            num_x,\n            num_cosets,\n            max_temp_bytes,\n        )\n    };\n    debug!(\"zerocheck:temp_sums_buffer_capacity={temp_sums_buffer_capacity}\");\n    let mut temp_sums_buffer = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(temp_sums_buffer_capacity);\n    let used_temp_bytes =\n        intermed_capacity * size_of::<F>() + temp_sums_buffer_capacity * size_of::<EF>();\n    if used_temp_bytes > max_temp_bytes {\n        // We do not error if the required bytes is greater than the requested max, but this may\n        // lead to unexpected peak memory usage.\n        warn!(\"zerocheck used_temp_bytes ({used_temp_bytes}) > max_temp_bytes ({max_temp_bytes})\");\n    }\n\n    let preprocessed_ptr = pk\n        .preprocessed_data\n        .as_ref()\n        .map(|cd| cd.trace.buffer().as_ptr())\n        .unwrap_or(std::ptr::null());\n\n    let mut sp_evals =\n        DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(num_cosets as usize * skip_domain as usize);\n    // SAFETY:\n    // - No bounds checks are done in this kernel. It fully assumes that the Rules are trusted and\n    //   all nodes are valid.\n    unsafe {\n        zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints(\n            &mut temp_sums_buffer,\n            &mut sp_evals,\n            selectors_cube,\n            preprocessed_ptr,\n            main_parts,\n            eq_cube,\n            lambda_pows,\n            public_values,\n            &rules.inner.d_rules,\n            &rules.inner.d_used_nodes,\n            buffer_size,\n            &mut intermediates,\n            skip_domain,\n            num_x,\n            height,\n            num_cosets,\n            g_shift,\n            max_temp_bytes,\n        )?;\n    }\n\n    Ok(sp_evals)\n}\n\n/// Evaluate interaction constraints (excluding plain AIR constraints) for a single AIR, given\n/// prepared trace input.\n///\n/// `constraints` includes interaction expressions for the AIR.\n/// See [`crate::logup_zerocheck`] module docs for async-free/peak memory behavior.\n#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\npub fn evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    beta_pows: &[EF],\n    eq_3bs: &[EF],\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, Round0EvalError> {\n    // Check if this trace has interactions\n    if eq_3bs.is_empty() {\n        return Ok(DeviceBuffer::new());\n    }\n    let large_domain = num_cosets * skip_domain;\n\n    // We create a new \"interactions DAG\" where the new .constraints are the interaction [count,\n    // message_0, message_1, ..] expressions themselves, while the .interactions are empty\n    // We track the indices with InteractionNode\n\n    // Copied from build_symbolic_constraints_dag to handle sorting of constraints\n    // NOTE: For logup round0, the kernel uses weights indexed by rule_idx, not constraint_idx.\n    // So we deduplicate constraint_idx and use dag_idx_to_rule_idx for weight mapping.\n    let (rules, d_numer_weights, d_denom_weights, denom_sum_init) = {\n        let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n        let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n        for interaction in &symbolic.interactions {\n            let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n            sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n            sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n                interaction\n                    .message\n                    .iter()\n                    .map(|field_expr| dag_builder.add_expr(field_expr)),\n            );\n        }\n        sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n        // Deduplicate for the dag since logup round0 kernel doesn't use used_nodes\n        sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n        let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n            nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n            constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n        };\n        let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n        let mut numer_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; rules.rules.len()];\n        let mut denom_weights = vec![EF::ZERO; rules.rules.len()];\n        let mut denom_sum_init = EF::ZERO;\n        for (interaction_idx, interaction) in symbolic.interactions.iter().enumerate() {\n            // CAUTION: an expression node could be used in multiple interactions, and might even be\n            // used as `count` in one, but message field in another. We only care about their\n            // weighted sum with eq_3b, so we compute the weights ahead of time.\n            let count_dag_idx =\n                dag_builder.expr_to_idx[&(&interaction.count as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n            let count_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&count_dag_idx];\n            numer_weights[count_rule_idx] += eq_3bs[interaction_idx];\n            denom_sum_init += eq_3bs[interaction_idx]\n                * beta_pows[interaction.message.len()]\n                * F::from_u32(interaction.bus_index as u32 + 1);\n\n            for (message_idx, message) in interaction.message.iter().enumerate() {\n                let message_dag_idx =\n                    dag_builder.expr_to_idx[&(message as *const SymbolicExpression<_>)];\n                let message_rule_idx = rules.dag_idx_to_rule_idx[&message_dag_idx];","numLines":200,"startLine":1,"totalLines":276}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Fu64okDRbdfFvoyXYuHoFM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see what allocations happen per-AIR in Round 0:\n\nIn `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`:\n1. `intermediates = DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` - GPU allocation\n2. `temp_sums_buffer = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(temp_sums_buffer_capacity)` - GPU allocation\n3. `sp_evals = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(num_cosets * skip_domain)` - GPU allocation\n\n\n4. `d_main_parts = main_parts.to_device()` - GPU allocation (H2D copy) in `process_air_round0`\n\nWith 8 threads each processing roughly 39 AIRs and each AIR triggering 6-8 allocations, that's hundreds of allocations per thread contending for the MemoryManager mutex, and the cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync calls are likely causing cross-stream synchronization issues.\n\nThe real question is whether I can pre-allocate these buffers per thread instead. The problem is that buffer sizes vary by AIR—`intermediates` and `temp_sums_buffer` depend on properties like `buffer_size`, `skip_domain`, `num_x`, and `num_cosets`, while `sp_evals` scales with `num_cosets * skip_domain`. I could compute the maximum size across all AIRs in the segment and allocate once per thread at that size, similar to what worked for GKR input eval.\n\nLooking at the performance data, Round 0 takes 296ms at APC 300 with seg0 and seg1 both at 148ms. That's interesting because it's different from GKR where seg0 dominated—here they're equal, which suggests seg1 might be hiding significant allocation overhead that pre-allocation could expose and eliminate.\n\nThe GKR input eval comparison is telling: before pre-allocation seg0 and seg1 were similar at 275ms and 257ms, but after pre-allocation seg1 dropped to 62ms while seg0 stayed at 256ms. That 4x improvement in seg1 shows the pattern clearly—when two segments have similar wall times despite different computational loads, the one with less actual work is overhead-dominated, and pre-allocation can unlock massive gains there.\n\nApplying this to Round 0, I'm estimating seg1 could drop from 148ms to 40-60ms with pre-allocation, giving us a 31-37% improvement on Round 0 alone and roughly 6-8% on the overall STARK. That's a solid win with high confidence since the pattern is already proven. I'm going to focus on pre-allocating per-thread GPU buffers for Round 0 evaluation as my top optimization target, and now I need to dig into the code to see exactly what buffers need to be allocated.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3107,"cache_read_input_tokens":95572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3107},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e16bd043-1446-4590-8b8f-e55946754639","uuid":"5ba6cd49-e515-488c-be0b-5209a008dba6"}
