{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ptaUrxfPffYyChfVxF2EF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-2300-batch-mle-round-kernels\n2\t\n3\tReplace the per-AIR kernel launch loop in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (stacked reduction MLE rounds) with batched kernel launches using descriptor arrays. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~600 AIR windows and launches one kernel per window (10K+ degenerate + 5K+ non-degenerate launches per benchmark), but total GPU compute is only 62ms while wall time is 182ms at APC 300. Batching all per-AIR launches into 1-2 kernel launches per round (using the proven descriptor array pattern from the stacking scatter kernel) will eliminate ~15K kernel launches, improve GPU SM utilization through concurrent block execution, and reduce CPU loop overhead — targeting a 50-100ms reduction in MLE Rounds time at APC 300.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e16bd043-1446-4590-8b8f-e55946754639","uuid":"fdbe151c-2609-41fd-8c81-3c324eabd6d4","timestamp":"2026-04-13T05:15:03.547Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-2300-batch-mle-round-kernels\n\nReplace the per-AIR kernel launch loop in `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (stacked reduction MLE rounds) with batched kernel launches using descriptor arrays. Currently, each MLE round iterates over ~600 AIR windows and launches one kernel per window (10K+ degenerate + 5K+ non-degenerate launches per benchmark), but total GPU compute is only 62ms while wall time is 182ms at APC 300. Batching all per-AIR launches into 1-2 kernel launches per round (using the proven descriptor array pattern from the stacking scatter kernel) will eliminate ~15K kernel launches, improve GPU SM utilization through concurrent block execution, and reduce CPU loop overhead — targeting a 50-100ms reduction in MLE Rounds time at APC 300.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
