{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AEQNRguZw4Qug21YVy8htP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread GPU buffers for Round 0\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-AIR `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` and `MemoryManager` mutex overhead in Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread GPU buffers. This is the same optimization pattern applied to GKR input eval in task `2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`, which achieved 1.67x improvement at APC 300 (532ms → 318ms).\n6\t\n7\tRound 0 currently takes 296ms at APC 300 (seg0=148ms, seg1=148ms). Each AIR allocates 6 temporary `DeviceBuffer`s via the global `Mutex<MemoryManager>` + `cudaMallocAsync`: zerocheck `intermediates`, `temp_sums_buffer`, `sp_evals`, and logup `intermediates`, `temp_sums_buffer`, `s_evals`. With ~310 AIRs per segment across 8 threads, this causes ~2,400 mutex acquisitions and ~2,400 `cudaFreeAsync` calls per segment. The `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` calls cause implicit CUDA memory pool cross-stream synchronization, serializing the 8 worker threads.\n8\t\n9\t**Expected improvement**: Round 0 296ms → ~190-220ms (~75-106ms reduction, 25-36%). STARK excl trace ~70-100ms improvement (5-7%). Based on GKR prealloc precedent where seg1 (many small AIRs, allocation-dominated) improved 4.15x while seg0 (few large AIRs, kernel-dominated) improved 1.07x.\n10\t\n11\t## Current Code Path\n12\t\n13\t### Entry point\n14\t`LogupZerocheckGpu::sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:765`\n15\t\n16\t### Phase 1: Build work items (lines 897-924)\n17\t- Creates `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` with read-only references per AIR\n18\t- Sets `max_temp_bytes = self.memory_limit_bytes / NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS` (line 898)\n19\t- Sorts by descending height for load balance (line 927)\n20\t\n21\t### Phase 2: Process AIRs in parallel (lines 933-964)\n22\t- If ≥ 100 AIRs: spawns `NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS` (8) OS threads via `std::thread::scope`\n23\t- Each thread calls `process_air_round0()` per AIR in its chunk\n24\t\n25\t### process_air_round0 (lines 138-269)\n26\tPer AIR, calls two functions that each allocate temporary GPU buffers:\n27\t\n28\t**evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu** (`round0.rs:31-124`):\n29\t1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n30\t2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>::with_capacity(temp_sums_capacity)` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n31\t3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>::with_capacity(num_cosets * skip_domain)` — output buffer (line 96)\n32\t4. Launches `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints()` kernel (line 101)\n33\t5. All three buffers freed on function return (Drop → cudaFreeAsync)\n34\t\n35\t**evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu** (`round0.rs:132-275`):\n36\t1. `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, `d_rules` — small H2D uploads per AIR (lines 204-210)\n37\t2. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n38\t3. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(temp_sums_capacity)` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n39\t4. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(large_domain)` — output buffer (line 248)\n40\t5. Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0()` kernel (line 251)\n41\t6. All buffers freed on function return\n42\t\n43\t### Per-AIR allocation count: 6 large allocations + 4 small H2D uploads = 10 GPU memory operations\n44\t### Per-segment at APC 300: ~310 AIRs × 10 = ~3,100 GPU memory operations\n45\t\n46\t## Changes\n47\t\n48\t### Change 1: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct\n49\t\n50\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n51\t\n52\tAdd a struct after `Round0AirWorkItem` (around line 137):\n53\t\n54\t```rust\n55\tstruct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n56\t    /// Pre-allocated buffer for zerocheck constraint intermediates\n57\t    zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n58\t    /// Pre-allocated buffer for zerocheck constraint temp_sums\n59\t    zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n60\t    /// Pre-allocated buffer for logup interaction intermediates\n61\t    logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n62\t    /// Pre-allocated buffer for logup interaction temp_sums\n63\t    logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n64\t}\n65\t```\n66\t\n67\tNote: we do NOT pre-allocate `sp_evals` (output of zerocheck) or `s_evals` (output of logup) because these are small (num_cosets × skip_domain elements, typically < 100) and must be returned to the caller. The allocation overhead for small buffers is negligible.\n68\t\n69\t### Change 2: Pre-compute max buffer sizes\n70\t\n71\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n72\t\n73\tAfter building `work_items` and before `current_stream_sync()` (between lines 924 and 929), add a max-size computation loop:\n74\t\n75\t```rust\n76\tlet mut max_zc_intermediates: usize = 0;\n77\tlet mut max_zc_temp_sums: usize = 0;\n78\tlet mut max_logup_intermediates: usize = 0;\n79\tlet mut max_logup_temp_sums: usize = 0;\n80\t\n81\tfor w in &work_items {\n82\t    let single_pk = w.single_pk;\n83\t    let local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n84\t    let n_lift = w.n.max(0) as usize;\n85\t    let num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n86\t    let num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg;\n87\t    let skip_domain = 1u32 << w.l_skip;\n88\t    let num_x = 1u32 << n_lift;\n89\t\n90\t    // Zerocheck constraint buffers\n91\t    let zc_rules = &single_pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0;\n92\t    if !single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints.constraints.constraint_idx.is_empty()\n93\t        && num_cosets_zc > 0\n94\t    {\n95\t        let buffer_size: u32 = zc_rules.inner.buffer_size;\n96\t        let zc_inter = unsafe {\n97\t            _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n98\t                buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n99\t            )\n100\t        };\n101\t        let zc_temp = unsafe {\n102\t            _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n103\t                buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n104\t            )\n105\t        };\n106\t        max_zc_intermediates = max_zc_intermediates.max(zc_inter);\n107\t        max_zc_temp_sums = max_zc_temp_sums.max(zc_temp);\n108\t    }\n109\t\n110\t    // Logup interaction buffers\n111\t    // Interaction rules are built per-AIR in evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu,\n112\t    // so we use the constraint buffer_size as an upper bound for logup intermediates.\n113\t    // The actual logup intermediates depend on the interaction DAG which varies per AIR.\n114\t    // We use max(height) * num_cosets_logup as a conservative upper bound for temp_sums.\n115\t    let has_interactions = !w.eq_3bs.is_empty();\n116\t    if has_interactions {\n117\t        // For logup intermediates/temp_sums, we cannot call the FFI size functions\n118\t        // directly because the interaction rules (SymbolicRulesGpu) are built per-AIR\n119\t        // inside evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu. Instead, we pre-build the interaction\n120\t        // rules for each AIR to get the buffer_size, then call the FFI functions.\n121\t        let symbolic = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n122\t        let (rules_buffer_size, _) = compute_logup_round0_buffer_size(&symbolic);\n123\t        let logup_inter = unsafe {\n124\t            _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n125\t                rules_buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_logup as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n126\t            )\n127\t        };\n128\t        let logup_temp = unsafe {\n129\t            _logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n130\t                rules_buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_logup as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n131\t            )\n132\t        };\n133\t        max_logup_intermediates = max_logup_intermediates.max(logup_inter);\n134\t        max_logup_temp_sums = max_logup_temp_sums.max(logup_temp);\n135\t    }\n136\t}\n137\t```\n138\t\n139\t**Issue**: The logup interaction rules are built per-AIR inside `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. To compute max logup buffer sizes, we need the `buffer_size` from `SymbolicRulesGpu`. We have two options:\n140\t\n141\t**Option A (simpler)**: Extract a small helper `compute_logup_round0_buffer_size(symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints) -> (u32, usize)` that builds the interaction DAG and returns only `(rules.buffer_size, rules.rules.len())`. This is CPU-only work, called on the main thread.\n142\t\n143\t**Option B (faster)**: Cache the `SymbolicRulesGpu` (or at least `buffer_size`) as part of `DeviceStarkProvingKey::other_data` at keygen time, alongside the existing `zerocheck_round0` rules. This avoids rebuilding the DAG at proving time.\n144\t\n145\t**Recommendation**: Use Option A for the initial implementation. The DAG building is fast (microseconds per AIR, ~310 × ~5us = ~1.5ms total). Option B can be a follow-up if profiling shows this matters.\n146\t\n147\t### Change 3: Add memory budget check and allocate per-thread buffers\n148\t\n149\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n150\t\n151\tAfter computing max sizes and before `current_stream_sync()`:\n152\t\n153\t```rust\n154\tlet per_thread_bytes =\n155\t    max_zc_intermediates * size_of::<F>()\n156\t    + max_zc_temp_sums * size_of::<EF>()\n157\t    + max_logup_intermediates * size_of::<F>()\n158\t    + max_logup_temp_sums * size_of::<Frac<EF>>();\n159\t\n160\tlet mut num_threads = if work_items.len() >= 100 {\n161\t    NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())\n162\t} else {\n163\t    1\n164\t};\n165\t\n166\t// Safety valve: reduce threads if pre-allocation would exceed 2 GB\n167\twhile num_threads > 1 && num_threads * per_thread_bytes > 2_000_000_000 {\n168\t    num_threads /= 2;\n169\t    tracing::warn!(\n170\t        \"Reducing Round 0 thread count to {} due to memory budget ({}MB per thread)\",\n171\t        num_threads,\n172\t        per_thread_bytes / (1024 * 1024)\n173\t    );\n174\t}\n175\t\n176\tlet thread_buffers: Vec<Round0ThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)\n177\t    .map(|_| Round0ThreadBuffers {\n178\t        zc_intermediates: if max_zc_intermediates > 0 {\n179\t            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_intermediates)\n180\t        } else {\n181\t            DeviceBuffer::new()\n182\t        },\n183\t        zc_temp_sums: if max_zc_temp_sums > 0 {\n184\t            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_temp_sums)\n185\t        } else {\n186\t            DeviceBuffer::new()\n187\t        },\n188\t        logup_intermediates: if max_logup_intermediates > 0 {\n189\t            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_intermediates)\n190\t        } else {\n191\t            DeviceBuffer::new()\n192\t        },\n193\t        logup_temp_sums: if max_logup_temp_sums > 0 {\n194\t            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_temp_sums)\n195\t        } else {\n196\t            DeviceBuffer::new()\n197\t        },\n198\t    })\n199\t    .collect();\n200\t```\n201\t\n202\t### Change 4: Modify `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` to accept pre-allocated buffers\n203\t\n204\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n205\t\n206\tChange the function signature to take optional pre-allocated buffers:\n207\t\n208\t```rust\n209\tpub fn evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n210\t    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n211\t    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n212\t    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n213\t    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n214\t    eq_cube: *const EF,\n215\t    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n216\t    skip_domain: u32,\n217\t    num_x: u32,\n218\t    height: u32,\n219\t    num_cosets: u32,\n220\t    g_shift: F,\n221\t    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n222\t    prealloc_intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,       // NEW\n223\t    prealloc_temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,          // NEW\n224\t) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<EF>, Round0EvalError> {\n225\t```\n226\t\n227\tInside the function, replace the allocation code:\n228\t- Replace `let mut intermediates = ... DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` with `let intermediates = prealloc_intermediates;` (using the pre-allocated buffer directly)\n229\t- Replace `let mut temp_sums_buffer = ... DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(...)` with `let temp_sums_buffer = prealloc_temp_sums;`\n230\t- Keep `sp_evals` allocation as-is (small output buffer that must be returned)\n231\t\n232\tThe pre-allocated buffers have capacity ≥ the required size since we took the max across all AIRs. The kernel writes only the needed portion. The `sp_evals` output buffer is still allocated per-AIR since it's small and returned.\n233\t\n234\t### Change 5: Modify `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` to accept pre-allocated buffers\n235\t\n236\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n237\t\n238\tSame pattern: add `prealloc_intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>` and `prealloc_temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` parameters.\n239\t\n240\tReplace the internal `intermediates` and `temp_sums_buffer` allocations with the pre-allocated buffers.\n241\t\n242\tKeep `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, `d_rules`, and `s_evals` allocations as-is — these are small per-AIR data that can't be reused.\n243\t\n244\t### Change 6: Update `process_air_round0` signature\n245\t\n246\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n247\t\n248\tChange `process_air_round0` to accept `&mut Round0ThreadBuffers`:\n249\t\n250\t```rust\n251\tfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n252\t    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n253\t    buffers: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n254\t) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError> {\n255\t```\n256\t\n257\tPass `&mut buffers.zc_intermediates` and `&mut buffers.zc_temp_sums` to `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`, and `&mut buffers.logup_intermediates` and `&mut buffers.logup_temp_sums` to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`.\n258\t\n259\t### Change 7: Update thread spawning to pass buffers\n260\t\n261\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n262\t\n263\tFollow the exact GKR prealloc pattern (from `gkr_input.rs` lines 323-349):\n264\t\n265\t```rust\n266\tif num_threads <= 1 {\n267\t    let mut bufs = thread_buffers.into_iter().next().unwrap();\n268\t    for w in &work_items {\n269\t        results.push(process_air_round0(w, &mut bufs)?);\n270\t    }\n271\t} else {\n272\t    let chunk_size = work_items.len().div_ceil(num_threads);\n273\t    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n274\t        let handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n275\t            .into_iter()\n276\t            .zip(work_items.chunks(chunk_size))\n277\t            .map(|(mut bufs, chunk)| {\n278\t                s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n279\t                    chunk\n280\t                        .iter()\n281\t                        .map(|w| process_air_round0(w, &mut bufs))\n282\t                        .collect()\n283\t                })\n284\t            })\n285\t            .collect();\n286\t        // ... collect results as before\n287\t    })?;\n288\t}\n289\t```\n290\t\n291\t### Change 8: Add helper function for logup buffer size computation\n292\t\n293\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n294\t\n295\tAdd a public helper that computes the logup round0 buffer_size without performing any GPU work:\n296\t\n297\t```rust\n298\t/// Compute the buffer_size for logup round0 interaction rules.\n299\t/// Returns (buffer_size_as_u32, rules_count).\n300\tpub fn compute_logup_round0_buffer_size(\n301\t    symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>,\n302\t) -> (u32, usize) {\n303\t    if symbolic.interactions.is_empty() {\n304\t        return (0, 0);\n305\t    }\n306\t    let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n307\t    let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n308\t    for interaction in &symbolic.interactions {\n309\t        let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n310\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n311\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n312\t            interaction.message.iter().map(|e| dag_builder.add_expr(e)),\n313\t        );\n314\t    }\n315\t    sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n316\t    sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n317\t    let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n318\t        nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n319\t        constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n320\t    };\n321\t    let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n322\t    (rules.buffer_size.try_into().unwrap(), rules.rules.len())\n323\t}\n324\t```\n325\t\n326\tThis is called once per AIR on the main thread during the max-size pre-computation (Change 2).\n327\t\n328\t## Invariants\n329\t\n330\t1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers must have capacity ≥ the required size for every AIR. The max-size computation ensures this. The kernels write only the needed portion and read using their own size parameters, so stale data in the buffer tail is never read.\n331\t\n332\t2. **Memory safety**: The `DeviceBuffer` backing memory must remain valid for the kernel's lifetime. Since pre-allocated buffers live for the entire Round 0 phase (not just one kernel launch), this is satisfied.\n333\t\n334\t3. **No APC 0 regression**: The `>= 100 AIR` threshold for multi-threading is preserved. APC 0 (~20 AIRs/segment) uses the sequential path with a single set of pre-allocated buffers.\n335\t\n336\t4. **Memory budget**: The 2 GB safety valve prevents OOM from large pre-allocations. If per-thread memory exceeds budget, thread count is halved (same pattern as GKR prealloc).\n337\t\n338\t5. **Output buffers unchanged**: `sp_evals` and `s_evals` are still allocated per-AIR and returned normally. Only internal temporary buffers are pre-allocated.\n339\t\n340\t6. **Kernel semantics unchanged**: The CUDA kernels receive the same pointer arguments. They don't care whether the backing buffer was allocated per-AIR or pre-allocated at max size; they only use the explicit size parameters passed to them.\n341\t\n342\t## Measurement Plan\n343\t\n344\tRun the standard benchmark suite:\n345\t```bash\n346\tcd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n347\t# APC 0, 100, 300\n348\tfor apc in apc000 apc100 apc300; do\n349\t    /path/to/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact ${apc}.cbor --input 0 \\\n350\t        --metrics after_${apc}/metrics.json --recursion\n351\tdone\n352\t```\n353\t\n354\tAnalyze with `spec.py` and compare:\n355\t\n356\t**Primary success criteria** (all must pass):\n357\t1. Round 0 at APC 300: < 240ms (at least 19% improvement from 296ms)\n358\t2. STARK excl trace at APC 300: < 1380ms (at least 4% improvement from 1442ms)\n359\t3. STARK excl trace at APC 0: < 2200ms (no regression)\n360\t\n361\t**Secondary targets**:\n362\t4. Round 0 seg1 at APC 300: < 100ms (expecting 50-70% reduction from 148ms due to allocation-dominated workload)\n363\t5. Round 0 at APC 100: < 210ms (improvement from 250ms)\n364\t\n365\t## Rollback Criteria\n366\t\n367\tRevert if ANY of these are true:\n368\t1. STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 40ms (< 2.8% of current 1442ms)\n369\t2. STARK excl trace at APC 0 regresses by more than 65ms\n370\t3. GPU OOM at any APC configuration\n371\t4. Prove+verify fails at any APC configuration\n372\t5. Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 30ms (< 10% of current 296ms)\n373\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e16bd043-1446-4590-8b8f-e55946754639","uuid":"bcd01500-ae24-409c-9c75-03ac8f413def","timestamp":"2026-04-13T08:01:14.553Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-prealloc-round0-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread GPU buffers for Round 0\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate per-AIR `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` and `MemoryManager` mutex overhead in Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread GPU buffers. This is the same optimization pattern applied to GKR input eval in task `2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`, which achieved 1.67x improvement at APC 300 (532ms → 318ms).\n\nRound 0 currently takes 296ms at APC 300 (seg0=148ms, seg1=148ms). Each AIR allocates 6 temporary `DeviceBuffer`s via the global `Mutex<MemoryManager>` + `cudaMallocAsync`: zerocheck `intermediates`, `temp_sums_buffer`, `sp_evals`, and logup `intermediates`, `temp_sums_buffer`, `s_evals`. With ~310 AIRs per segment across 8 threads, this causes ~2,400 mutex acquisitions and ~2,400 `cudaFreeAsync` calls per segment. The `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` calls cause implicit CUDA memory pool cross-stream synchronization, serializing the 8 worker threads.\n\n**Expected improvement**: Round 0 296ms → ~190-220ms (~75-106ms reduction, 25-36%). STARK excl trace ~70-100ms improvement (5-7%). Based on GKR prealloc precedent where seg1 (many small AIRs, allocation-dominated) improved 4.15x while seg0 (few large AIRs, kernel-dominated) improved 1.07x.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Entry point\n`LogupZerocheckGpu::sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:765`\n\n### Phase 1: Build work items (lines 897-924)\n- Creates `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` with read-only references per AIR\n- Sets `max_temp_bytes = self.memory_limit_bytes / NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS` (line 898)\n- Sorts by descending height for load balance (line 927)\n\n### Phase 2: Process AIRs in parallel (lines 933-964)\n- If ≥ 100 AIRs: spawns `NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS` (8) OS threads via `std::thread::scope`\n- Each thread calls `process_air_round0()` per AIR in its chunk\n\n### process_air_round0 (lines 138-269)\nPer AIR, calls two functions that each allocate temporary GPU buffers:\n\n**evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu** (`round0.rs:31-124`):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>::with_capacity(temp_sums_capacity)` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>::with_capacity(num_cosets * skip_domain)` — output buffer (line 96)\n4. Launches `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints()` kernel (line 101)\n5. All three buffers freed on function return (Drop → cudaFreeAsync)\n\n**evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu** (`round0.rs:132-275`):\n1. `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, `d_rules` — small H2D uploads per AIR (lines 204-210)\n2. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n3. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(temp_sums_capacity)` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n4. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(large_domain)` — output buffer (line 248)\n5. Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0()` kernel (line 251)\n6. All buffers freed on function return\n\n### Per-AIR allocation count: 6 large allocations + 4 small H2D uploads = 10 GPU memory operations\n### Per-segment at APC 300: ~310 AIRs × 10 = ~3,100 GPU memory operations\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 1: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd a struct after `Round0AirWorkItem` (around line 137):\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n    /// Pre-allocated buffer for zerocheck constraint intermediates\n    zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated buffer for zerocheck constraint temp_sums\n    zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated buffer for logup interaction intermediates\n    logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated buffer for logup interaction temp_sums\n    logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n}\n```\n\nNote: we do NOT pre-allocate `sp_evals` (output of zerocheck) or `s_evals` (output of logup) because these are small (num_cosets × skip_domain elements, typically < 100) and must be returned to the caller. The allocation overhead for small buffers is negligible.\n\n### Change 2: Pre-compute max buffer sizes\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter building `work_items` and before `current_stream_sync()` (between lines 924 and 929), add a max-size computation loop:\n\n```rust\nlet mut max_zc_intermediates: usize = 0;\nlet mut max_zc_temp_sums: usize = 0;\nlet mut max_logup_intermediates: usize = 0;\nlet mut max_logup_temp_sums: usize = 0;\n\nfor w in &work_items {\n    let single_pk = w.single_pk;\n    let local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n    let n_lift = w.n.max(0) as usize;\n    let num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n    let num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg;\n    let skip_domain = 1u32 << w.l_skip;\n    let num_x = 1u32 << n_lift;\n\n    // Zerocheck constraint buffers\n    let zc_rules = &single_pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0;\n    if !single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints.constraints.constraint_idx.is_empty()\n        && num_cosets_zc > 0\n    {\n        let buffer_size: u32 = zc_rules.inner.buffer_size;\n        let zc_inter = unsafe {\n            _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n                buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n            )\n        };\n        let zc_temp = unsafe {\n            _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n                buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n            )\n        };\n        max_zc_intermediates = max_zc_intermediates.max(zc_inter);\n        max_zc_temp_sums = max_zc_temp_sums.max(zc_temp);\n    }\n\n    // Logup interaction buffers\n    // Interaction rules are built per-AIR in evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu,\n    // so we use the constraint buffer_size as an upper bound for logup intermediates.\n    // The actual logup intermediates depend on the interaction DAG which varies per AIR.\n    // We use max(height) * num_cosets_logup as a conservative upper bound for temp_sums.\n    let has_interactions = !w.eq_3bs.is_empty();\n    if has_interactions {\n        // For logup intermediates/temp_sums, we cannot call the FFI size functions\n        // directly because the interaction rules (SymbolicRulesGpu) are built per-AIR\n        // inside evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu. Instead, we pre-build the interaction\n        // rules for each AIR to get the buffer_size, then call the FFI functions.\n        let symbolic = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n        let (rules_buffer_size, _) = compute_logup_round0_buffer_size(&symbolic);\n        let logup_inter = unsafe {\n            _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n                rules_buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_logup as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n            )\n        };\n        let logup_temp = unsafe {\n            _logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n                rules_buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_logup as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n            )\n        };\n        max_logup_intermediates = max_logup_intermediates.max(logup_inter);\n        max_logup_temp_sums = max_logup_temp_sums.max(logup_temp);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Issue**: The logup interaction rules are built per-AIR inside `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. To compute max logup buffer sizes, we need the `buffer_size` from `SymbolicRulesGpu`. We have two options:\n\n**Option A (simpler)**: Extract a small helper `compute_logup_round0_buffer_size(symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints) -> (u32, usize)` that builds the interaction DAG and returns only `(rules.buffer_size, rules.rules.len())`. This is CPU-only work, called on the main thread.\n\n**Option B (faster)**: Cache the `SymbolicRulesGpu` (or at least `buffer_size`) as part of `DeviceStarkProvingKey::other_data` at keygen time, alongside the existing `zerocheck_round0` rules. This avoids rebuilding the DAG at proving time.\n\n**Recommendation**: Use Option A for the initial implementation. The DAG building is fast (microseconds per AIR, ~310 × ~5us = ~1.5ms total). Option B can be a follow-up if profiling shows this matters.\n\n### Change 3: Add memory budget check and allocate per-thread buffers\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter computing max sizes and before `current_stream_sync()`:\n\n```rust\nlet per_thread_bytes =\n    max_zc_intermediates * size_of::<F>()\n    + max_zc_temp_sums * size_of::<EF>()\n    + max_logup_intermediates * size_of::<F>()\n    + max_logup_temp_sums * size_of::<Frac<EF>>();\n\nlet mut num_threads = if work_items.len() >= 100 {\n    NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())\n} else {\n    1\n};\n\n// Safety valve: reduce threads if pre-allocation would exceed 2 GB\nwhile num_threads > 1 && num_threads * per_thread_bytes > 2_000_000_000 {\n    num_threads /= 2;\n    tracing::warn!(\n        \"Reducing Round 0 thread count to {} due to memory budget ({}MB per thread)\",\n        num_threads,\n        per_thread_bytes / (1024 * 1024)\n    );\n}\n\nlet thread_buffers: Vec<Round0ThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)\n    .map(|_| Round0ThreadBuffers {\n        zc_intermediates: if max_zc_intermediates > 0 {\n            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_intermediates)\n        } else {\n            DeviceBuffer::new()\n        },\n        zc_temp_sums: if max_zc_temp_sums > 0 {\n            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_temp_sums)\n        } else {\n            DeviceBuffer::new()\n        },\n        logup_intermediates: if max_logup_intermediates > 0 {\n            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_intermediates)\n        } else {\n            DeviceBuffer::new()\n        },\n        logup_temp_sums: if max_logup_temp_sums > 0 {\n            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_temp_sums)\n        } else {\n            DeviceBuffer::new()\n        },\n    })\n    .collect();\n```\n\n### Change 4: Modify `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` to accept pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nChange the function signature to take optional pre-allocated buffers:\n\n```rust\npub fn evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n    prealloc_intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,       // NEW\n    prealloc_temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,          // NEW\n) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<EF>, Round0EvalError> {\n```\n\nInside the function, replace the allocation code:\n- Replace `let mut intermediates = ... DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` with `let intermediates = prealloc_intermediates;` (using the pre-allocated buffer directly)\n- Replace `let mut temp_sums_buffer = ... DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(...)` with `let temp_sums_buffer = prealloc_temp_sums;`\n- Keep `sp_evals` allocation as-is (small output buffer that must be returned)\n\nThe pre-allocated buffers have capacity ≥ the required size since we took the max across all AIRs. The kernel writes only the needed portion. The `sp_evals` output buffer is still allocated per-AIR since it's small and returned.\n\n### Change 5: Modify `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` to accept pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nSame pattern: add `prealloc_intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>` and `prealloc_temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` parameters.\n\nReplace the internal `intermediates` and `temp_sums_buffer` allocations with the pre-allocated buffers.\n\nKeep `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, `d_rules`, and `s_evals` allocations as-is — these are small per-AIR data that can't be reused.\n\n### Change 6: Update `process_air_round0` signature\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nChange `process_air_round0` to accept `&mut Round0ThreadBuffers`:\n\n```rust\nfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n    buffers: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError> {\n```\n\nPass `&mut buffers.zc_intermediates` and `&mut buffers.zc_temp_sums` to `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`, and `&mut buffers.logup_intermediates` and `&mut buffers.logup_temp_sums` to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`.\n\n### Change 7: Update thread spawning to pass buffers\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nFollow the exact GKR prealloc pattern (from `gkr_input.rs` lines 323-349):\n\n```rust\nif num_threads <= 1 {\n    let mut bufs = thread_buffers.into_iter().next().unwrap();\n    for w in &work_items {\n        results.push(process_air_round0(w, &mut bufs)?);\n    }\n} else {\n    let chunk_size = work_items.len().div_ceil(num_threads);\n    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n        let handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n            .into_iter()\n            .zip(work_items.chunks(chunk_size))\n            .map(|(mut bufs, chunk)| {\n                s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n                    chunk\n                        .iter()\n                        .map(|w| process_air_round0(w, &mut bufs))\n                        .collect()\n                })\n            })\n            .collect();\n        // ... collect results as before\n    })?;\n}\n```\n\n### Change 8: Add helper function for logup buffer size computation\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd a public helper that computes the logup round0 buffer_size without performing any GPU work:\n\n```rust\n/// Compute the buffer_size for logup round0 interaction rules.\n/// Returns (buffer_size_as_u32, rules_count).\npub fn compute_logup_round0_buffer_size(\n    symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>,\n) -> (u32, usize) {\n    if symbolic.interactions.is_empty() {\n        return (0, 0);\n    }\n    let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n    let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n    for interaction in &symbolic.interactions {\n        let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n        sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n        sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n            interaction.message.iter().map(|e| dag_builder.add_expr(e)),\n        );\n    }\n    sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n    sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n    let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n        nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n        constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n    };\n    let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n    (rules.buffer_size.try_into().unwrap(), rules.rules.len())\n}\n```\n\nThis is called once per AIR on the main thread during the max-size pre-computation (Change 2).\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers must have capacity ≥ the required size for every AIR. The max-size computation ensures this. The kernels write only the needed portion and read using their own size parameters, so stale data in the buffer tail is never read.\n\n2. **Memory safety**: The `DeviceBuffer` backing memory must remain valid for the kernel's lifetime. Since pre-allocated buffers live for the entire Round 0 phase (not just one kernel launch), this is satisfied.\n\n3. **No APC 0 regression**: The `>= 100 AIR` threshold for multi-threading is preserved. APC 0 (~20 AIRs/segment) uses the sequential path with a single set of pre-allocated buffers.\n\n4. **Memory budget**: The 2 GB safety valve prevents OOM from large pre-allocations. If per-thread memory exceeds budget, thread count is halved (same pattern as GKR prealloc).\n\n5. **Output buffers unchanged**: `sp_evals` and `s_evals` are still allocated per-AIR and returned normally. Only internal temporary buffers are pre-allocated.\n\n6. **Kernel semantics unchanged**: The CUDA kernels receive the same pointer arguments. They don't care whether the backing buffer was allocated per-AIR or pre-allocated at max size; they only use the explicit size parameters passed to them.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\nRun the standard benchmark suite:\n```bash\ncd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n# APC 0, 100, 300\nfor apc in apc000 apc100 apc300; do\n    /path/to/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact ${apc}.cbor --input 0 \\\n        --metrics after_${apc}/metrics.json --recursion\ndone\n```\n\nAnalyze with `spec.py` and compare:\n\n**Primary success criteria** (all must pass):\n1. Round 0 at APC 300: < 240ms (at least 19% improvement from 296ms)\n2. STARK excl trace at APC 300: < 1380ms (at least 4% improvement from 1442ms)\n3. STARK excl trace at APC 0: < 2200ms (no regression)\n\n**Secondary targets**:\n4. Round 0 seg1 at APC 300: < 100ms (expecting 50-70% reduction from 148ms due to allocation-dominated workload)\n5. Round 0 at APC 100: < 210ms (improvement from 250ms)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\nRevert if ANY of these are true:\n1. STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 40ms (< 2.8% of current 1442ms)\n2. STARK excl trace at APC 0 regresses by more than 65ms\n3. GPU OOM at any APC configuration\n4. Prove+verify fails at any APC configuration\n5. Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 30ms (< 10% of current 296ms)\n","numLines":373,"startLine":1,"totalLines":373}}}
