{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DEHiiEKeBhYhLWUK6Cgcpn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread GPU buffers for Round 0\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tEliminate per-AIR `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` and `MemoryManager` mutex overhead in Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread GPU buffers. This is the same optimization pattern applied to GKR input eval in task `2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`, which achieved 1.67x improvement at APC 300 (532ms → 318ms).\n6\t\n7\tRound 0 currently takes 296ms at APC 300 (seg0=148ms, seg1=148ms). Each AIR allocates 4 large temporary `DeviceBuffer`s via the global `Mutex<MemoryManager>` + `cudaMallocAsync` (zerocheck `intermediates` and `temp_sums_buffer`, logup `intermediates` and `temp_sums_buffer`), plus 2 small output buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) and 4 small H2D uploads (`d_main_parts`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, `d_rules`). With ~310 AIRs per segment across 8 threads, the 4 large temporaries alone cause ~2,480 alloc/free pairs per segment. The `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` calls cause implicit CUDA memory pool cross-stream synchronization, serializing the 8 worker threads.\n8\t\n9\t**Expected improvement**: Round 0 296ms → ~190-220ms (~75-106ms reduction, 25-36%). STARK excl trace ~70-100ms improvement (5-7%). Based on GKR prealloc precedent where seg1 (many small AIRs, allocation-dominated) improved 4.15x while seg0 (few large AIRs, kernel-dominated) improved 1.07x.\n10\t\n11\t## Current Code Path\n12\t\n13\t### Entry point\n14\t`LogupZerocheckGpu::sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:765`\n15\t\n16\t### Phase 1: Build work items (lines 897-924)\n17\t- Creates `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` with read-only references per AIR\n18\t- Sets `max_temp_bytes = self.memory_limit_bytes / NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS` (line 898)\n19\t- Sorts by descending height for load balance (line 927)\n20\t\n21\t### Phase 2: Process AIRs in parallel (lines 933-964)\n22\t- If ≥ 100 AIRs: spawns `NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS` (8) OS threads via `std::thread::scope`\n23\t- Each thread calls `process_air_round0()` per AIR in its chunk\n24\t\n25\t### process_air_round0 (lines 138-269)\n26\tPer AIR, calls two functions that each allocate temporary GPU buffers:\n27\t\n28\t**evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu** (`round0.rs:31-124`):\n29\t1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n30\t2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>::with_capacity(temp_sums_capacity)` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n31\t3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>::with_capacity(num_cosets * skip_domain)` — output buffer (line 96)\n32\t4. Launches `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints()` kernel (line 101)\n33\t5. All three buffers freed on function return (Drop → cudaFreeAsync)\n34\t\n35\t**evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu** (`round0.rs:132-275`):\n36\t1. `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, `d_rules` — small H2D uploads per AIR (lines 204-210)\n37\t2. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n38\t3. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(temp_sums_capacity)` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n39\t4. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(large_domain)` — output buffer (line 248)\n40\t5. Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0()` kernel (line 251)\n41\t6. All buffers freed on function return\n42\t\n43\t### Per-AIR allocation count: 4 large temporary allocations + 2 small output allocations + 4 small H2D uploads = 10 GPU memory operations\n44\t### Per-segment at APC 300: ~310 AIRs × 10 = ~3,100 GPU memory operations (pre-allocation targets the 4 large temporaries = ~1,240 alloc/free pairs per segment)\n45\t\n46\t## Changes\n47\t\n48\t### Change 1: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct and extend `Round0AirWorkItem`\n49\t\n50\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n51\t\n52\tAdd a struct after `Round0AirWorkItem` (around line 137):\n53\t\n54\t```rust\n55\tstruct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n56\t    /// Pre-allocated buffer for zerocheck constraint intermediates\n57\t    zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n58\t    /// Pre-allocated buffer for zerocheck constraint temp_sums\n59\t    zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n60\t    /// Pre-allocated buffer for logup interaction intermediates\n61\t    logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n62\t    /// Pre-allocated buffer for logup interaction temp_sums\n63\t    logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n64\t}\n65\t```\n66\t\n67\tAdd a field to `Round0AirWorkItem`:\n68\t\n69\t```rust\n70\t/// Pre-computed logup round0 interaction rules buffer_size (from SymbolicRulesGpu).\n71\t/// Computed once during work item construction to avoid rebuilding the DAG per-AIR\n72\t/// both during max-size pre-computation and inside evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu.\n73\tlogup_r0_buffer_size: u32,\n74\t```\n75\t\n76\tCompute this field when building work items (inside the `.map()` at line 907):\n77\t\n78\t```rust\n79\tlet logup_r0_buffer_size = if !eq3b.is_empty() {\n80\t    let symbolic = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n81\t    compute_logup_round0_buffer_size(&symbolic).0\n82\t} else {\n83\t    0\n84\t};\n85\t```\n86\t\n87\tThis pre-computation allows the max-size loop (Change 2) to compute logup buffer sizes without needing its own `SymbolicConstraints::from()` call per AIR. Note: `process_air_round0` still does `SymbolicConstraints::from()` at line 142 because `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` needs the full symbolic constraints for weight computation and rule encoding — only the `buffer_size` lookup is cached.\n88\t\n89\tNote: we do NOT pre-allocate `sp_evals` (output of zerocheck) or `s_evals` (output of logup) because these are small (num_cosets × skip_domain elements, typically < 100) and must be returned to the caller. The allocation overhead for small buffers is negligible.\n90\t\n91\t### Change 2: Pre-compute max buffer sizes\n92\t\n93\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n94\t\n95\tAfter building `work_items` and before `current_stream_sync()` (between lines 924 and 929), add a max-size computation loop:\n96\t\n97\t```rust\n98\tlet mut max_zc_intermediates: usize = 0;\n99\tlet mut max_zc_temp_sums: usize = 0;\n100\tlet mut max_logup_intermediates: usize = 0;\n101\tlet mut max_logup_temp_sums: usize = 0;\n102\t\n103\tfor w in &work_items {\n104\t    let single_pk = w.single_pk;\n105\t    let local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n106\t    let n_lift = w.n.max(0) as usize;\n107\t    let num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n108\t    let num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg;\n109\t    let skip_domain = 1u32 << w.l_skip;\n110\t    let num_x = 1u32 << n_lift;\n111\t\n112\t    // Zerocheck constraint buffers\n113\t    let zc_rules = &single_pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0;\n114\t    if !single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints.constraints.constraint_idx.is_empty()\n115\t        && num_cosets_zc > 0\n116\t    {\n117\t        let buffer_size: u32 = zc_rules.inner.buffer_size;\n118\t        let zc_inter = unsafe {\n119\t            _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n120\t                buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n121\t            )\n122\t        };\n123\t        let zc_temp = unsafe {\n124\t            _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n125\t                buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n126\t            )\n127\t        };\n128\t        max_zc_intermediates = max_zc_intermediates.max(zc_inter);\n129\t        max_zc_temp_sums = max_zc_temp_sums.max(zc_temp);\n130\t    }\n131\t\n132\t    // Logup interaction buffers — use the pre-computed logup_r0_buffer_size from Change 1\n133\t    if w.logup_r0_buffer_size > 0 {\n134\t        let logup_inter = unsafe {\n135\t            _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n136\t                w.logup_r0_buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_logup as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n137\t            )\n138\t        };\n139\t        let logup_temp = unsafe {\n140\t            _logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n141\t                w.logup_r0_buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_logup as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n142\t            )\n143\t        };\n144\t        max_logup_intermediates = max_logup_intermediates.max(logup_inter);\n145\t        max_logup_temp_sums = max_logup_temp_sums.max(logup_temp);\n146\t    }\n147\t}\n148\t```\n149\t\n150\tNote: `logup_r0_buffer_size` is computed once per work item in Change 1 via `compute_logup_round0_buffer_size()`. This avoids a separate `SymbolicConstraints::from()` call in this loop.\n151\t\n152\t### Change 3: Add memory budget check and allocate per-thread buffers\n153\t\n154\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n155\t\n156\tAfter computing max sizes and before `current_stream_sync()`:\n157\t\n158\t```rust\n159\tlet per_thread_bytes =\n160\t    max_zc_intermediates * size_of::<F>()\n161\t    + max_zc_temp_sums * size_of::<EF>()\n162\t    + max_logup_intermediates * size_of::<F>()\n163\t    + max_logup_temp_sums * size_of::<Frac<EF>>();\n164\t\n165\tlet mut num_threads = if work_items.len() >= 100 {\n166\t    NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())\n167\t} else {\n168\t    1\n169\t};\n170\t\n171\t// Safety valve: reduce threads if pre-allocation would exceed 2 GB\n172\twhile num_threads > 1 && num_threads * per_thread_bytes > 2_000_000_000 {\n173\t    num_threads /= 2;\n174\t    tracing::warn!(\n175\t        \"Reducing Round 0 thread count to {} due to memory budget ({}MB per thread)\",\n176\t        num_threads,\n177\t        per_thread_bytes / (1024 * 1024)\n178\t    );\n179\t}\n180\t\n181\tlet thread_buffers: Vec<Round0ThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)\n182\t    .map(|_| Round0ThreadBuffers {\n183\t        zc_intermediates: if max_zc_intermediates > 0 {\n184\t            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_intermediates)\n185\t        } else {\n186\t            DeviceBuffer::new()\n187\t        },\n188\t        zc_temp_sums: if max_zc_temp_sums > 0 {\n189\t            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_temp_sums)\n190\t        } else {\n191\t            DeviceBuffer::new()\n192\t        },\n193\t        logup_intermediates: if max_logup_intermediates > 0 {\n194\t            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_intermediates)\n195\t        } else {\n196\t            DeviceBuffer::new()\n197\t        },\n198\t        logup_temp_sums: if max_logup_temp_sums > 0 {\n199\t            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_temp_sums)\n200\t        } else {\n201\t            DeviceBuffer::new()\n202\t        },\n203\t    })\n204\t    .collect();\n205\t```\n206\t\n207\t### Change 4: Modify `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` to accept pre-allocated buffers\n208\t\n209\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n210\t\n211\tChange the function signature to take optional pre-allocated buffers:\n212\t\n213\t```rust\n214\tpub fn evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n215\t    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n216\t    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n217\t    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n218\t    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n219\t    eq_cube: *const EF,\n220\t    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n221\t    skip_domain: u32,\n222\t    num_x: u32,\n223\t    height: u32,\n224\t    num_cosets: u32,\n225\t    g_shift: F,\n226\t    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n227\t    prealloc_intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,       // NEW\n228\t    prealloc_temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,          // NEW\n229\t) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<EF>, Round0EvalError> {\n230\t```\n231\t\n232\tInside the function, replace the allocation code:\n233\t- Replace `let mut intermediates = ... DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` with `let intermediates = prealloc_intermediates;` (using the pre-allocated buffer directly)\n234\t- Replace `let mut temp_sums_buffer = ... DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(...)` with `let temp_sums_buffer = prealloc_temp_sums;`\n235\t- Keep `sp_evals` allocation as-is (small output buffer that must be returned)\n236\t\n237\tThe pre-allocated buffers have capacity ≥ the required size since we took the max across all AIRs. The kernel writes only the needed portion. The `sp_evals` output buffer is still allocated per-AIR since it's small and returned.\n238\t\n239\t### Change 5: Modify `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` to accept pre-allocated buffers\n240\t\n241\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n242\t\n243\tAdd `prealloc_intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>` and `prealloc_temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` parameters. Do NOT pass `logup_r0_buffer_size` — the function still builds the full DAG and rules per-AIR (needed for `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, weight index mapping), so it obtains `buffer_size` from `rules.buffer_size` naturally. The pre-computed `logup_r0_buffer_size` is only needed in the max-size computation loop (Change 2).\n244\t\n245\tReplace the internal `intermediates` and `temp_sums_buffer` allocations with the pre-allocated buffers.\n246\t\n247\tKeep `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, `d_rules`, and `s_evals` allocations as-is — these are small per-AIR data that can't be reused.\n248\t\n249\t### Change 6: Update `process_air_round0` signature\n250\t\n251\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n252\t\n253\tChange `process_air_round0` to accept `&mut Round0ThreadBuffers`:\n254\t\n255\t```rust\n256\tfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n257\t    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n258\t    buffers: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n259\t) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError> {\n260\t```\n261\t\n262\tPass `&mut buffers.zc_intermediates` and `&mut buffers.zc_temp_sums` to `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`, and `&mut buffers.logup_intermediates` and `&mut buffers.logup_temp_sums` to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`.\n263\t\n264\t### Change 7: Update thread spawning to pass buffers\n265\t\n266\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n267\t\n268\tFollow the exact GKR prealloc pattern (from `gkr_input.rs` lines 323-349):\n269\t\n270\t```rust\n271\tif num_threads <= 1 {\n272\t    let mut bufs = thread_buffers.into_iter().next().unwrap();\n273\t    for w in &work_items {\n274\t        results.push(process_air_round0(w, &mut bufs)?);\n275\t    }\n276\t} else {\n277\t    let chunk_size = work_items.len().div_ceil(num_threads);\n278\t    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n279\t        let handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n280\t            .into_iter()\n281\t            .zip(work_items.chunks(chunk_size))\n282\t            .map(|(mut bufs, chunk)| {\n283\t                s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n284\t                    chunk\n285\t                        .iter()\n286\t                        .map(|w| process_air_round0(w, &mut bufs))\n287\t                        .collect()\n288\t                })\n289\t            })\n290\t            .collect();\n291\t        // ... collect results as before\n292\t    })?;\n293\t}\n294\t```\n295\t\n296\t### Change 8: Add helper function for logup buffer size computation\n297\t\n298\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n299\t\n300\tAdd a public helper that computes the logup round0 buffer_size without performing any GPU work:\n301\t\n302\t```rust\n303\t/// Compute the buffer_size for logup round0 interaction rules.\n304\t/// Returns (buffer_size_as_u32, rules_count).\n305\tpub fn compute_logup_round0_buffer_size(\n306\t    symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>,\n307\t) -> (u32, usize) {\n308\t    if symbolic.interactions.is_empty() {\n309\t        return (0, 0);\n310\t    }\n311\t    let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n312\t    let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n313\t    for interaction in &symbolic.interactions {\n314\t        let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n315\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n316\t        sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n317\t            interaction.message.iter().map(|e| dag_builder.add_expr(e)),\n318\t        );\n319\t    }\n320\t    sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n321\t    sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n322\t    let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n323\t        nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n324\t        constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n325\t    };\n326\t    let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n327\t    (rules.buffer_size.try_into().unwrap(), rules.rules.len())\n328\t}\n329\t```\n330\t\n331\tThis is called once per AIR on the main thread during work item construction (Change 1). The returned `buffer_size` is stored in `Round0AirWorkItem::logup_r0_buffer_size` and reused in the max-size pre-computation loop (Change 2), keeping that loop simple without needing its own `SymbolicConstraints::from()` call per AIR.\n332\t\n333\t## Invariants\n334\t\n335\t1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers must have capacity ≥ the required size for every AIR. The max-size computation ensures this. The kernels write only the needed portion and read using their own size parameters, so stale data in the buffer tail is never read.\n336\t\n337\t2. **Memory safety**: The `DeviceBuffer` backing memory must remain valid for the kernel's lifetime. Since pre-allocated buffers live for the entire Round 0 phase (not just one kernel launch), this is satisfied.\n338\t\n339\t3. **No APC 0 regression**: The `>= 100 AIR` threshold for multi-threading is preserved. APC 0 (~20 AIRs/segment) uses the sequential path with a single set of pre-allocated buffers.\n340\t\n341\t4. **Memory budget**: The 2 GB safety valve prevents OOM from large pre-allocations. If per-thread memory exceeds budget, thread count is halved (same pattern as GKR prealloc).\n342\t\n343\t5. **Output buffers unchanged**: `sp_evals` and `s_evals` are still allocated per-AIR and returned normally. Only internal temporary buffers are pre-allocated.\n344\t\n345\t6. **Kernel semantics unchanged**: The CUDA kernels receive the same pointer arguments. They don't care whether the backing buffer was allocated per-AIR or pre-allocated at max size; they only use the explicit size parameters passed to them.\n346\t\n347\t## Measurement Plan\n348\t\n349\tRun the standard benchmark suite:\n350\t```bash\n351\tcd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n352\t# APC 0, 100, 300\n353\tfor apc in apc000 apc100 apc300; do\n354\t    /path/to/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact ${apc}.cbor --input 0 \\\n355\t        --metrics after_${apc}/metrics.json --recursion\n356\tdone\n357\t```\n358\t\n359\tAnalyze with `spec.py` and compare:\n360\t\n361\t**Primary success criteria** (all must pass):\n362\t1. Round 0 at APC 300: < 240ms (at least 19% improvement from 296ms)\n363\t2. STARK excl trace at APC 300: < 1380ms (at least 4% improvement from 1442ms)\n364\t3. STARK excl trace at APC 0: < 2200ms (no regression)\n365\t\n366\t**Secondary targets**:\n367\t4. Round 0 seg1 at APC 300: < 100ms (expecting 50-70% reduction from 148ms due to allocation-dominated workload)\n368\t5. Round 0 at APC 100: < 210ms (improvement from 250ms)\n369\t\n370\t## Rollback Criteria\n371\t\n372\tRevert if ANY of these are true:\n373\t1. STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 40ms (< 2.8% of current 1442ms)\n374\t2. STARK excl trace at APC 0 regresses by more than 65ms\n375\t3. GPU OOM at any APC configuration\n376\t4. Prove+verify fails at any APC configuration\n377\t5. Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 30ms (< 10% of current 296ms)\n378\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e16bd043-1446-4590-8b8f-e55946754639","uuid":"a73dfe4c-0fb0-4137-b92b-777ab56f1993","timestamp":"2026-04-13T08:08:41.190Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-prealloc-round0-buffers/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Pre-allocate per-thread GPU buffers for Round 0\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate per-AIR `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` and `MemoryManager` mutex overhead in Round 0 constraint and interaction evaluation by pre-allocating reusable per-thread GPU buffers. This is the same optimization pattern applied to GKR input eval in task `2026-04-13-2100-prealloc-gkr-input-buffers`, which achieved 1.67x improvement at APC 300 (532ms → 318ms).\n\nRound 0 currently takes 296ms at APC 300 (seg0=148ms, seg1=148ms). Each AIR allocates 4 large temporary `DeviceBuffer`s via the global `Mutex<MemoryManager>` + `cudaMallocAsync` (zerocheck `intermediates` and `temp_sums_buffer`, logup `intermediates` and `temp_sums_buffer`), plus 2 small output buffers (`sp_evals`, `s_evals`) and 4 small H2D uploads (`d_main_parts`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, `d_rules`). With ~310 AIRs per segment across 8 threads, the 4 large temporaries alone cause ~2,480 alloc/free pairs per segment. The `cudaMallocAsync`/`cudaFreeAsync` calls cause implicit CUDA memory pool cross-stream synchronization, serializing the 8 worker threads.\n\n**Expected improvement**: Round 0 296ms → ~190-220ms (~75-106ms reduction, 25-36%). STARK excl trace ~70-100ms improvement (5-7%). Based on GKR prealloc precedent where seg1 (many small AIRs, allocation-dominated) improved 4.15x while seg0 (few large AIRs, kernel-dominated) improved 1.07x.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Entry point\n`LogupZerocheckGpu::sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` at `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:765`\n\n### Phase 1: Build work items (lines 897-924)\n- Creates `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` with read-only references per AIR\n- Sets `max_temp_bytes = self.memory_limit_bytes / NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS` (line 898)\n- Sorts by descending height for load balance (line 927)\n\n### Phase 2: Process AIRs in parallel (lines 933-964)\n- If ≥ 100 AIRs: spawns `NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS` (8) OS threads via `std::thread::scope`\n- Each thread calls `process_air_round0()` per AIR in its chunk\n\n### process_air_round0 (lines 138-269)\nPer AIR, calls two functions that each allocate temporary GPU buffers:\n\n**evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu** (`round0.rs:31-124`):\n1. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 63-68)\n2. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<EF>::with_capacity(temp_sums_capacity)` — size from `_zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 80)\n3. `sp_evals: DeviceBuffer<EF>::with_capacity(num_cosets * skip_domain)` — output buffer (line 96)\n4. Launches `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints()` kernel (line 101)\n5. All three buffers freed on function return (Drop → cudaFreeAsync)\n\n**evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu** (`round0.rs:132-275`):\n1. `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, `d_rules` — small H2D uploads per AIR (lines 204-210)\n2. `intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` — size from `_logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size()` (line 222-227)\n3. `temp_sums_buffer: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(temp_sums_capacity)` — size from `_logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size()` (line 233)\n4. `s_evals: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(large_domain)` — output buffer (line 248)\n5. Launches `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0()` kernel (line 251)\n6. All buffers freed on function return\n\n### Per-AIR allocation count: 4 large temporary allocations + 2 small output allocations + 4 small H2D uploads = 10 GPU memory operations\n### Per-segment at APC 300: ~310 AIRs × 10 = ~3,100 GPU memory operations (pre-allocation targets the 4 large temporaries = ~1,240 alloc/free pairs per segment)\n\n## Changes\n\n### Change 1: Add `Round0ThreadBuffers` struct and extend `Round0AirWorkItem`\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAdd a struct after `Round0AirWorkItem` (around line 137):\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n    /// Pre-allocated buffer for zerocheck constraint intermediates\n    zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated buffer for zerocheck constraint temp_sums\n    zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    /// Pre-allocated buffer for logup interaction intermediates\n    logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    /// Pre-allocated buffer for logup interaction temp_sums\n    logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n}\n```\n\nAdd a field to `Round0AirWorkItem`:\n\n```rust\n/// Pre-computed logup round0 interaction rules buffer_size (from SymbolicRulesGpu).\n/// Computed once during work item construction to avoid rebuilding the DAG per-AIR\n/// both during max-size pre-computation and inside evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu.\nlogup_r0_buffer_size: u32,\n```\n\nCompute this field when building work items (inside the `.map()` at line 907):\n\n```rust\nlet logup_r0_buffer_size = if !eq3b.is_empty() {\n    let symbolic = SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n    compute_logup_round0_buffer_size(&symbolic).0\n} else {\n    0\n};\n```\n\nThis pre-computation allows the max-size loop (Change 2) to compute logup buffer sizes without needing its own `SymbolicConstraints::from()` call per AIR. Note: `process_air_round0` still does `SymbolicConstraints::from()` at line 142 because `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` needs the full symbolic constraints for weight computation and rule encoding — only the `buffer_size` lookup is cached.\n\nNote: we do NOT pre-allocate `sp_evals` (output of zerocheck) or `s_evals` (output of logup) because these are small (num_cosets × skip_domain elements, typically < 100) and must be returned to the caller. The allocation overhead for small buffers is negligible.\n\n### Change 2: Pre-compute max buffer sizes\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter building `work_items` and before `current_stream_sync()` (between lines 924 and 929), add a max-size computation loop:\n\n```rust\nlet mut max_zc_intermediates: usize = 0;\nlet mut max_zc_temp_sums: usize = 0;\nlet mut max_logup_intermediates: usize = 0;\nlet mut max_logup_temp_sums: usize = 0;\n\nfor w in &work_items {\n    let single_pk = w.single_pk;\n    let local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n    let n_lift = w.n.max(0) as usize;\n    let num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n    let num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg;\n    let skip_domain = 1u32 << w.l_skip;\n    let num_x = 1u32 << n_lift;\n\n    // Zerocheck constraint buffers\n    let zc_rules = &single_pk.other_data.zerocheck_round0;\n    if !single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints.constraints.constraint_idx.is_empty()\n        && num_cosets_zc > 0\n    {\n        let buffer_size: u32 = zc_rules.inner.buffer_size;\n        let zc_inter = unsafe {\n            _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n                buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n            )\n        };\n        let zc_temp = unsafe {\n            _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n                buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_zc as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n            )\n        };\n        max_zc_intermediates = max_zc_intermediates.max(zc_inter);\n        max_zc_temp_sums = max_zc_temp_sums.max(zc_temp);\n    }\n\n    // Logup interaction buffers — use the pre-computed logup_r0_buffer_size from Change 1\n    if w.logup_r0_buffer_size > 0 {\n        let logup_inter = unsafe {\n            _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(\n                w.logup_r0_buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_logup as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n            )\n        };\n        let logup_temp = unsafe {\n            _logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(\n                w.logup_r0_buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, num_cosets_logup as u32, w.max_temp_bytes,\n            )\n        };\n        max_logup_intermediates = max_logup_intermediates.max(logup_inter);\n        max_logup_temp_sums = max_logup_temp_sums.max(logup_temp);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nNote: `logup_r0_buffer_size` is computed once per work item in Change 1 via `compute_logup_round0_buffer_size()`. This avoids a separate `SymbolicConstraints::from()` call in this loop.\n\n### Change 3: Add memory budget check and allocate per-thread buffers\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nAfter computing max sizes and before `current_stream_sync()`:\n\n```rust\nlet per_thread_bytes =\n    max_zc_intermediates * size_of::<F>()\n    + max_zc_temp_sums * size_of::<EF>()\n    + max_logup_intermediates * size_of::<F>()\n    + max_logup_temp_sums * size_of::<Frac<EF>>();\n\nlet mut num_threads = if work_items.len() >= 100 {\n    NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS.min(work_items.len())\n} else {\n    1\n};\n\n// Safety valve: reduce threads if pre-allocation would exceed 2 GB\nwhile num_threads > 1 && num_threads * per_thread_bytes > 2_000_000_000 {\n    num_threads /= 2;\n    tracing::warn!(\n        \"Reducing Round 0 thread count to {} due to memory budget ({}MB per thread)\",\n        num_threads,\n        per_thread_bytes / (1024 * 1024)\n    );\n}\n\nlet thread_buffers: Vec<Round0ThreadBuffers> = (0..num_threads)\n    .map(|_| Round0ThreadBuffers {\n        zc_intermediates: if max_zc_intermediates > 0 {\n            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_intermediates)\n        } else {\n            DeviceBuffer::new()\n        },\n        zc_temp_sums: if max_zc_temp_sums > 0 {\n            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_zc_temp_sums)\n        } else {\n            DeviceBuffer::new()\n        },\n        logup_intermediates: if max_logup_intermediates > 0 {\n            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_intermediates)\n        } else {\n            DeviceBuffer::new()\n        },\n        logup_temp_sums: if max_logup_temp_sums > 0 {\n            DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(max_logup_temp_sums)\n        } else {\n            DeviceBuffer::new()\n        },\n    })\n    .collect();\n```\n\n### Change 4: Modify `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` to accept pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nChange the function signature to take optional pre-allocated buffers:\n\n```rust\npub fn evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n    prealloc_intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>,       // NEW\n    prealloc_temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<EF>,          // NEW\n) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<EF>, Round0EvalError> {\n```\n\nInside the function, replace the allocation code:\n- Replace `let mut intermediates = ... DeviceBuffer::<F>::with_capacity(intermed_capacity)` with `let intermediates = prealloc_intermediates;` (using the pre-allocated buffer directly)\n- Replace `let mut temp_sums_buffer = ... DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(...)` with `let temp_sums_buffer = prealloc_temp_sums;`\n- Keep `sp_evals` allocation as-is (small output buffer that must be returned)\n\nThe pre-allocated buffers have capacity ≥ the required size since we took the max across all AIRs. The kernel writes only the needed portion. The `sp_evals` output buffer is still allocated per-AIR since it's small and returned.\n\n### Change 5: Modify `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` to accept pre-allocated buffers\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd `prealloc_intermediates: &mut DeviceBuffer<F>` and `prealloc_temp_sums: &mut DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>` parameters. Do NOT pass `logup_r0_buffer_size` — the function still builds the full DAG and rules per-AIR (needed for `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, weight index mapping), so it obtains `buffer_size` from `rules.buffer_size` naturally. The pre-computed `logup_r0_buffer_size` is only needed in the max-size computation loop (Change 2).\n\nReplace the internal `intermediates` and `temp_sums_buffer` allocations with the pre-allocated buffers.\n\nKeep `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights`, `d_rules`, and `s_evals` allocations as-is — these are small per-AIR data that can't be reused.\n\n### Change 6: Update `process_air_round0` signature\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nChange `process_air_round0` to accept `&mut Round0ThreadBuffers`:\n\n```rust\nfn process_air_round0<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    w: &Round0AirWorkItem<HS>,\n    buffers: &mut Round0ThreadBuffers,\n) -> Result<Round0AirResult, LogupZerocheckError> {\n```\n\nPass `&mut buffers.zc_intermediates` and `&mut buffers.zc_temp_sums` to `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`, and `&mut buffers.logup_intermediates` and `&mut buffers.logup_temp_sums` to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`.\n\n### Change 7: Update thread spawning to pass buffers\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n\nFollow the exact GKR prealloc pattern (from `gkr_input.rs` lines 323-349):\n\n```rust\nif num_threads <= 1 {\n    let mut bufs = thread_buffers.into_iter().next().unwrap();\n    for w in &work_items {\n        results.push(process_air_round0(w, &mut bufs)?);\n    }\n} else {\n    let chunk_size = work_items.len().div_ceil(num_threads);\n    std::thread::scope(|s| {\n        let handles: Vec<_> = thread_buffers\n            .into_iter()\n            .zip(work_items.chunks(chunk_size))\n            .map(|(mut bufs, chunk)| {\n                s.spawn(move || -> Result<Vec<Round0AirResult>, LogupZerocheckError> {\n                    chunk\n                        .iter()\n                        .map(|w| process_air_round0(w, &mut bufs))\n                        .collect()\n                })\n            })\n            .collect();\n        // ... collect results as before\n    })?;\n}\n```\n\n### Change 8: Add helper function for logup buffer size computation\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n\nAdd a public helper that computes the logup round0 buffer_size without performing any GPU work:\n\n```rust\n/// Compute the buffer_size for logup round0 interaction rules.\n/// Returns (buffer_size_as_u32, rules_count).\npub fn compute_logup_round0_buffer_size(\n    symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>,\n) -> (u32, usize) {\n    if symbolic.interactions.is_empty() {\n        return (0, 0);\n    }\n    let mut dag_builder = SymbolicDagBuilder::new();\n    let mut sorted_used_dag_idxs = Vec::new();\n    for interaction in &symbolic.interactions {\n        let count = dag_builder.add_expr(&interaction.count);\n        sorted_used_dag_idxs.push(count);\n        sorted_used_dag_idxs.extend(\n            interaction.message.iter().map(|e| dag_builder.add_expr(e)),\n        );\n    }\n    sorted_used_dag_idxs.sort();\n    sorted_used_dag_idxs.dedup();\n    let dag = SymbolicExpressionDag {\n        nodes: dag_builder.nodes,\n        constraint_idx: sorted_used_dag_idxs,\n    };\n    let rules = SymbolicRulesGpu::new(&dag, true);\n    (rules.buffer_size.try_into().unwrap(), rules.rules.len())\n}\n```\n\nThis is called once per AIR on the main thread during work item construction (Change 1). The returned `buffer_size` is stored in `Round0AirWorkItem::logup_r0_buffer_size` and reused in the max-size pre-computation loop (Change 2), keeping that loop simple without needing its own `SymbolicConstraints::from()` call per AIR.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Correctness**: Pre-allocated buffers must have capacity ≥ the required size for every AIR. The max-size computation ensures this. The kernels write only the needed portion and read using their own size parameters, so stale data in the buffer tail is never read.\n\n2. **Memory safety**: The `DeviceBuffer` backing memory must remain valid for the kernel's lifetime. Since pre-allocated buffers live for the entire Round 0 phase (not just one kernel launch), this is satisfied.\n\n3. **No APC 0 regression**: The `>= 100 AIR` threshold for multi-threading is preserved. APC 0 (~20 AIRs/segment) uses the sequential path with a single set of pre-allocated buffers.\n\n4. **Memory budget**: The 2 GB safety valve prevents OOM from large pre-allocations. If per-thread memory exceeds budget, thread count is halved (same pattern as GKR prealloc).\n\n5. **Output buffers unchanged**: `sp_evals` and `s_evals` are still allocated per-AIR and returned normally. Only internal temporary buffers are pre-allocated.\n\n6. **Kernel semantics unchanged**: The CUDA kernels receive the same pointer arguments. They don't care whether the backing buffer was allocated per-AIR or pre-allocated at max size; they only use the explicit size parameters passed to them.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\nRun the standard benchmark suite:\n```bash\ncd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n# APC 0, 100, 300\nfor apc in apc000 apc100 apc300; do\n    /path/to/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact ${apc}.cbor --input 0 \\\n        --metrics after_${apc}/metrics.json --recursion\ndone\n```\n\nAnalyze with `spec.py` and compare:\n\n**Primary success criteria** (all must pass):\n1. Round 0 at APC 300: < 240ms (at least 19% improvement from 296ms)\n2. STARK excl trace at APC 300: < 1380ms (at least 4% improvement from 1442ms)\n3. STARK excl trace at APC 0: < 2200ms (no regression)\n\n**Secondary targets**:\n4. Round 0 seg1 at APC 300: < 100ms (expecting 50-70% reduction from 148ms due to allocation-dominated workload)\n5. Round 0 at APC 100: < 210ms (improvement from 250ms)\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\nRevert if ANY of these are true:\n1. STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 40ms (< 2.8% of current 1442ms)\n2. STARK excl trace at APC 0 regresses by more than 65ms\n3. GPU OOM at any APC configuration\n4. Prove+verify fails at any APC configuration\n5. Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 30ms (< 10% of current 296ms)\n","numLines":378,"startLine":1,"totalLines":378}}}
